  "notes": {
    "why": "the user, 2026-11-16: 「俄洛伊的头发一会有一会儿没很奇怪看起来」 - her run frames 1-2 (Codex's run2 / run3) drew a big mass of dreadlocks streaming back from a raised bun with gold rings, frames 0 and 3 almost none, so the hair popped in and out every 140 ms; League's Illaoi carries that mass behind her head in every animation (Illaoi_Run1: always there, swaying)",
    "dreads": "one picture: run frame 1's bun (the part above the design's head) and dreadlocks (the column behind the head and the mass streaming down-left), with the back-of-head hair squares, and three tapered dread ends drawn under the mass where frame 1's idol hid them - laid UNDER every frame (only clear squares) on the design head (anchor: the face, the design's head pasted in every key pose); the frames' own hair stays on top, so a pose that already draws the mass (run 1-2, ult 4-5, the death's stagger) gains only its margins",
    "bend": "the run's frames 0 and 3 (the hair falling as the body rises) 2 rows at the tip, the idol held overhead (attack 2, ult 3) 3: the mass droops instead of sticking out (root column 9: the bun and the column behind the head never move)",
    "run": "the run's own hair is in its drawn run (assets/source/illaoi/hd/illaoi_run_*: this part laid on the installed hd_run / run / lo_run with bends 2 0 0 2 - tools/art/run_body_anim.py makes the run from it), so `tags` leaves the run out",
    "flash": "hit 0 and dead 0 are flashed frames: their anchors set by hand (the next frame's, moved by the frames' rect sizes), the part tinted as ppu_rig.flash tints"
  },
